.TH INSTALL-NOTIFY-DNS-UPDATER 1 "August 2026" "mu2edaq-notify 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
install\-notify\-dns\-updater.sh \- install the self\-registering DNS updater on the AWS proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/install\-notify\-dns\-updater.sh
[\fB\-\-emit\-user\-data\fR]
[\fB\-\-gzip\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-caddyfile\fR]
[\fB\-H\fR \fIHOST\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIUSER\fR]
[\fB\-k\fR \fIKEYFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-timer\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Puts
.BR mu2edaq-notify-dns-update (1),
its configuration, its systemd unit and timer, the
.B caddy.service
ordering drop\-in and
.I /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
onto the EC2 proxy instance. All six come from the repo
.RI ( scripts/aws\-notify\-dns\-update.sh
and
.IR config/aws/ ),
which is the only copy under test.
.PP
The Caddyfile is validated with
.B caddy validate
before it replaces the installed one, and a running Caddy is reloaded rather
than restarted. A stopped Caddy is left stopped: starting it is ordered after
the DNS update.
.PP
Two modes:
.TP
default
Pipe a generated installer over SSH to a running instance, then enable the unit
and timer and run the updater once. The target address is taken from the EC2
API, since the instance no longer has a fixed one.
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-user\-data
Print a complete cloud\-init document \(en Caddy install, then the DNS updater
install, then
.B systemctl start caddy
\(en on standard output, for rebuilding the instance from scratch. That order
matters: Caddy answers the ACME HTTP\-01 challenge on this host's public
address, so it must not start before the record has been moved to that address.
.PP
Do not hand\-edit the installed copies. Edit the repo files and re\-run this,
or regenerate the user\-data; a pasted copy drifts from the tested one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-user\-data
Print the cloud\-init document and exit. The document is about 16.5 KB, which
is over EC2's 16384\-byte user\-data limit, so plain output is for review and
.B \-\-gzip
is the form to deploy. A warning is printed to standard error when the document
exceeds the limit.
.TP
.B \-\-gzip
Emit the document gzipped (about 6 KB). cloud\-init decompresses gzipped
user\-data; pass it to EC2 as
.BR fileb:// ,
and review it with
.BR "gunzip \-c" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-caddyfile
Leave
.I /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
alone.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fIHOST\fR
Target address. Default: the instance's current public IPv4 from the EC2 API.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
SSH user. Default
.BR ec2\-user .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEYFILE\fR
SSH private key. Default
.IR data/mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.pem .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-timer
Install the boot unit but not the five\-minute drift timer.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-run
Install and enable, but do not run the updater immediately.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install onto the running instance:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/install\-notify\-dns\-updater.sh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Regenerate user\-data for a rebuild and review it before use:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/install\-notify\-dns\-updater.sh \-\-emit\-user\-data \-\-gzip > /tmp/user\-data.gz
gunzip \-c /tmp/user\-data.gz | bash \-n
aws ec2 modify\-instance\-attribute \\
  \-\-instance\-id i\-000ee813ecd9a47b3 \\
  \-\-user\-data fileb:///tmp/user\-data.gz
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-notify-dns-update (1),
.BR update-notify-dns.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-caa.sh (1)
